• when you provide us with feedback;
• when you change your content or email preferences;
• when you respond to surveys and/or promotions;
• from public sources and information (including the internet).
We may receive personal information from third parties. If we do, we will protect it as set out in this Policy.
‍(b) Dispensed may contact you by a variety of measures including, but not limited to telephone, email, SMS or mail.
‍4. Purposes of collection and use of your personal information
We may collect and/or use your personal information for a variety of purposes, including, but not limited to, the purposes listed below:
• providing quality healthcare services, including but not limited to assessing, diagnosing and treating illnesses and medical conditions;
• disclosure to others involved in your health care, including doctors and clinicians outside of Dispensed (e.g. through referral to other clinicians, or for medical tests and in the reports or results returned to Dispensed following the referrals).
• providing follow-up reminder/recall notices for treatment and preventative healthcare which are often issued by SMS.
• providing you with products, services and/or any treatment requested by you;
• responding to your issues, inquiries or complaints;
• managing our relationship with you and providing you with information and updates regarding our business, products and services and new or additional products, services and opportunities available to you and generally managing and accounting for our products and services;
• improving our products and services and/or better understanding your needs;
• For the purposes of research only where de-identified information is used and to allow medical students and staff to participate in medical training/teaching (using only de-identified information).
• To comply with any legislative or regulatory requirements, e.g. notifiable diseases.
• Administrative purposes in relation to the operations of Dispensed as well as billing purposes;
